          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            %strong Top
            denotes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            and whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
            between them. Its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
            are the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphisms"} homeomorphisms
          %p
            For exposition see
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Topology+--+1"} Introduction to point-set topology
          %p
            Often one considers (sometimes by default)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategories"} subcategories
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nice+topological+spaces"} nice topological spaces
            such as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convenient+categories+of+topological+spaces"} convenient categories of topological spaces
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
            given by its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
            at the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalences"} weak homotopy equivalences
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+homotopy+category"} classical homotopy category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ho%28Top%29"} Ho(Top)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+localization"} simplicial localization
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            at the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalences"} weak homotopy equivalences
            is the archetypical
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"} equivalent
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            (see at
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+hypothesis"} homotopy hypothesis
