                  of the underlying diagram of sets, and whose topology is the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/final+topology"} final topology
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InitialAndFinalTopologies"}
                  for the component maps
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ι
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota_i
                  of the colimiting
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocone"} cocone
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi S
                                  %mi i
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo ⟶
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi S
                                  %mi j
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mrow
                                  %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %msub
                                        %mi ι
                                        %mi i
                                %mo ↘
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mo ↙
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %msub
                                        %mi ι
                                        %mi j
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %munder
                                    %mi lim
                                    %mo ⟶
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi i
                                    %mo ∈
                                    %mi I
                                %msub
                                  %mi S
                                  %mi i
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        S_i &amp;&amp; \longrightarrow &amp;&amp; S_j
                        \\\
                        \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{\iota_i}}\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{\iota_j}}
                        \\\
                        \&amp;&amp; \underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim}_{i \in I} S_i
                        }
                        \\,.
                %p Hence
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %munder
                            %mi lim
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi i
                        %mo ≃
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %msub
                            %munder
                              %mi lim
                              %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi I
                          %msub
                            %mi S
                            %mi i
                          %mo ,
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %msub
                            %mi τ
                            %mi final
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %msub
                            %mi ι
                            %mi i
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi I
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim}_{i \in I} X_i
                        \\simeq
                        \\left(\underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim}_{i \in I} S_i,\; \tau_{final}(\{\iota_i\}_{i \in I})\right)
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Bourbaki71"} Bourbaki 71, section I.4
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The required
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi τ
                        %mi initial
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left(\underset{\longleftarrow}{\lim}_{i \in I} S_i,\; \tau_{initial}(\{p_i\}_{i \in I})\right)
              is immediate: for
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi S
                            %mo ,
                            %mi τ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi f
                                    %mi i
                            %mo ↙
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi f
                                    %mi j
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi i
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; (S,\tau)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{f_i}}\swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{f_j}}
                    \\\
                    X_i &amp;&amp; \underset{}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp; X_j
                    }
            %p
              any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cone"} cone
              over the diagram, then by construction there is a unique function of underlying sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %munder
                        %mi lim
                        %mo ⟵
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \longrightarrow \underset{\longleftarrow}{\lim}_{i \in I} S_i
              making the required diagrams commute, and so all that is required is that this unique function is always
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous
            %p
              The case of the colimit is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formally dual
          #PointTopologicalSpaceAsEmptyLimit.num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              The limit over the empty diagram in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast
              with its unique topology.
          #DisjointUnionOfTopologicalSpacesIsCoproduct.num_example
            %h6#example_4 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{X_i\}_{i \in I}
              a set of topological spaces, their
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{i \in I}{\sqcup} X_i \in Top
              is their
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
          %p In particular:
          #DiscreteTopologicalSpaceAsCoproduct.num_example
            %h6#example_5 Example
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in Set
              = succeed "-indexed" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              of the point,
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                        %mrow
                          %mi s
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi S
                      %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{s \in S}{\coprod}\ast
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              itself equipped with the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/final+topology"} final topology
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+topological+space"} discrete topological space
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          #ProductTopologicalSpace.num_example
            %h6#example_6 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{X_i\}_{i \in I}
              a set of topological spaces, their
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{i \in I}{\prod} X_i \in Top
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
              of the underlying sets equipped with the
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topology"} product topology
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tychonoff+product"} Tychonoff product
            %p
              In the case that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite set
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times Y
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basis+for+a+topology"} sub-basis
              for the product topology is given by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+products"} Cartesian products
              of the open subsets of (a basis for) each factor space.
          #EqualizerInTop.num_example
            %h6#example_7 Example
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equalizer"} equalizer
              of two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ⟶
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f, g \colon X \stackrel{\longrightarrow}{\longrightarrow} Y
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
              is the equalizer of the underlying functions of sets
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi eq
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi X
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi g
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    eq(f,g)
                    \\hookrightarrow
                    S_X
                    \\stackrel{\overset{f}{\longrightarrow}}{\underset{g}{\longrightarrow}}
                    S_Y
            %p
              (hence the largets subset of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_X
              on which both functions coincide) and equipped with the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace+topology"} subspace topology
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalSubspace"}
          #CoequalizerInTop.num_example
            %h6#example_8 Example
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizer"} coequalizer
              of two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ⟶
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f, g \colon X \stackrel{\longrightarrow}{\longrightarrow} Y
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
              is the coequalizer of the underlying functions of sets
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi X
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi g
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi Y
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi coeq
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S_X
                    \\stackrel{\overset{f}{\longrightarrow}}{\underset{g}{\longrightarrow}}
                    S_Y
                    \\longrightarrow
                    coeq(f,g)
            %p
              (hence the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+set"} quotient set
              by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
              generated by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∼
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) \sim g(x)
              for all
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+topology"} quotient topology
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#QuotientTopology"}
          #PushoutInTop.num_example
            %h6#example_9 Example
            %p For
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi g
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\overset{g}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{f}}\downarrow
                    \\\
                    X
                    }
            %p
              two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
              out of the same
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              under this diagram is also called the
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi g
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi g
                                    %mo *
                                  %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %msub
                              %mo ⊔
                              %mi A
                            %mi Y
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo .
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\overset{g}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{f}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{g_\ast f}}
                    \\\
                    X &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X \sqcup_A Y
                    \\,.
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              (Here
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mo *
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_\ast f
              is also called the pushout of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} cobase change
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              along
              = succeed ".)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              is an inclusion, one also write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo ∪
                      %mi f
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \cup_f Y
              and calls this the
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/attaching+space"} attaching space
            %div{:style => "float:left;margin:0 10px 10px 0;"}
